  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Sodium borate (borax) is an antiinfective used in ophthalmology, i.e. for eye infections. It is an approved drug, though details of where and how widely it is used are not given in the available facts.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q5319&quot;>Wikidata Q5319</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>sodium borate</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>S01AX07</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB14505&quot;>DB14505</a></td></tr><tr><td>PubChem CID:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/16211214&quot;>16211214</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q5319&quot;>Q5319</a></td></tr><tr><td>formula:</td><td>B4H20Na2O17</td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>381.363 g/mol (PubChem)</td></tr></table></body></html>"));
